INSERT INTO `meeting_minutes` (`id`, `meeting_id`, `minutes`, `created_at`, `personnel`, `update_at`) VALUES
(1, 1008, '<p><strong>JESUS ENTHRONED NETWORK MINUTES FOR THE MEETING HELD ON 21ST 2025 TO 22RD APRIL 2025.</strong></p><p><i><strong>Members Present</strong></i></p><ol><li>Benjamin Kimani – Chairperson</li><li>Paul Muteti – Vice Chairperson</li><li>James Kiarie – Media Director</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><i><strong>In attendance&nbsp;</strong></i></p><ol><li>Michael Kamau – Member</li></ol><p><i><strong>Meeting Agenda</strong></i></p><ol><li>Opening</li><li>Review of the previous meeting</li><li>Preliminaries and arising issues</li><li>The Media Department</li><li>The Conference Committee</li><li>Prayers</li><li>Monthly program line-up</li><li>Tuesday Fellowship and Discipleship</li><li>Finance</li><li>August Prayers</li><li>2025 December Conference</li><li>Organization Registration</li><li>Remaining Visits</li><li>Travelling To Uganda</li><li>Any Other Business</li><li>Adjournment</li></ol><p><strong>OPENING</strong></p><p>The meeting began with a visit to Bishop Mungai at his residence, where members agreed to visit him and receive counsel and guidance on the same. With the Absence of James Kiarie who was not able to attend to logistic issues the other two members visited the Bishop and were guided appropriately. Later on the following day before the meeting resumed, the members had a prayer session for at least 2 and a half hours. They spent the time seeking clarity and receiving instruction and guidance from the Holy Spirit.</p><p>Some of the things confirmed during the prayer session are as follows.</p><ol><li>The trust that God has given us to transform a generation.</li><li>The strength and the grace available to actually fulfil God’s Agenda</li><li>The Acronym for the word Grace—God’s Righteousness And Character Expressed</li><li>The springs coming out,</li><li>The elevation of our voice, that the hearts of men are tuned to our voice.</li><li>Provision, where God shall send he will provide.</li><li>The confirmation of the vision where stars come together, streams join to form a river.</li><li>The overshadowing of the earthly wisdom. Among others</li></ol><p><strong>MIN/1/4/25: REVIEW OF THE PREVIOUS MEETING MINUTES.</strong></p><p>The previous meeting minutes were read by James Kiarie, confirmed by Benjamin Kimani and Seconded by Paul Muteti.</p><p><strong>MIN/2/4/25: PRELIMINARIES AND MATTERS ARISING.</strong></p><p>At the conclusion of the reading of the minutes, the members noted things scheduled to done that were not done. To begin with the schedule of the monthly programs had changed which was discussed later on its own. The calendar of events had changed also mostly at the High School reach-outs. That was scheduled to be properly planned in the coming year, 2026. Members also noted that on finance we were behind, members had not fully contributed as earlier on discussed, therefore running on a deficit. Members agreed to contribute even for the missing months in order to cater for future expenses. Other matters arising were discussed as individual agendas, such as the conference committee, the December conference, etc.</p><p><strong>MIN/3/4/25: THE MEDIA DEPARTMENT</strong></p><p>The Media department was appreciated for the good work done. Posters for the fellowships were done on time except on some few occasions where the poster was delayed. Also, the follow-up platform that had been made to manage cells, and members as well the content was coming right up well. On the issue of the Logo, the media department had not fully settled and was waiting for a design as at that time for comparison purposes. They had also requested to get the objectives of the December conference to begin planning and the tag line for the Logo.&nbsp;</p><p>The members discussed and came up with the conference objectives which were discussed under the December conference agenda. The tag line for logo also was discussed which the members settled at <strong>Kingdom, Unity Purpose</strong> representing the whole vision of the organization.</p><p>In addition, the media department requested for clarification on the materials needed for the Conference, including the Instruments and machines. The members agreed not to purchase anything this year and for the meantime lease whatever was required for the conference. The conference committee will come up with the budget for the same.</p><p><strong>MIN/4/4/25: THE CONFERENCE COMMITTEE</strong></p><p>The previously discussed committee was disbanded due to various reasons and a new committee formed. Benjamin was tasked with the responsibility of confirming the available of the members listed and planning their first meeting to discuss on the same.</p><p>The proposed committee included.</p><ol><li>Benjamin Kimani – Committee Chairperson</li><li>James Kiarie – Media Representative</li><li>Ruth Wanjiku – Music Representative (<i>To be confirmed by Benjamin)</i></li><li>Harvesta Maribe --&nbsp; Logistics and Planning</li><li>____________ -- Finance Secretary ( To be filled)</li><li>Gordon Omondi – Ushering Representative</li><li>Naomi Mwihaki – Committee Secretary</li><li>Raymond Kibet – Gilgil V.O.G Representative</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Benjamin was given to confirm the availability of the above mentioned people before or on 1st May 2025 so as to facilitate the planning of their first meeting.</p><p><strong>MIN/5/4/25: PRAYERS</strong></p><p>The current prayer coordinator, Paul Muteti, gave a review of prayer for the last quarter. Night Vigil were halted due to availability concerns on Friday, due to other commitments. Also, concerns were also raised on the agreed time to begin prayer during the Tuesday sessions which is 20:00HRS (08:00PM East African Time) members have not been consistently joining and were urged to do so for the same.</p><p>Regarding the next quarter to the August Conference, intense prayers were planned. Members were requested to pick 3 days of fast in a week where they will be praying for the conference in December. Also, members were requested to pick a day during their days of fast where they are to meet with a group of cell leaders for virtual prayers.</p><p>The prayer coordinator also said that he will be training the cell leaders in prayers by giving them an opportunity to lead prayers once in a month during the Tuesday Sessions. One cell leader alternatively will be given the opportunity to lead prayer during the sessions once in a month.&nbsp;</p><p>The instructions for the prayers for the next quarter were to be incorporated into the platform, Thee prayer coordinator promised to send them by May to the Media department.</p><p>This prayers will begin in May.</p><p><strong>MIN/6/4/25: MONTHLY PROGRAM LINE-UP</strong></p><p>Previously the program was lined up to have 3 sessions teaching basic doctrines, two consecutive sessions on exhortation messages, and one session on weekends to handle Question and Answer. The members agreed to do away with the Q&amp;A sessions due to the cell leaders meetings planned every Saturday. The members agreed to have the following schedule</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>DAY OF THE MONTH</td><td>TIME</td><td>SESSION</td><td>PURPOSE</td></tr><tr><td>Every Tuesday</td><td>8:00PM EAT-10:00PM EAT</td><td>Word Session</td><td>Teaching</td></tr><tr><td>Every Saturday</td><td><p>9:00 PM</p><p>10:00 PM EAT</p></td><td>Cell Leaders Meeting</td><td>Passing the Heart of God concerning the vision</td></tr><tr><td>After Every One Sunday</td><td><p>9:00PM –&nbsp;</p><p>10:00PM EAT</p></td><td>Media Meeting</td><td>Planning and Sensitizing Media Department</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>MIN/7/4/25: TUESDAY FELLOWSHIPS AND DISCIPLESHIP</strong></p><p>The discipleship Coordinator, Benjamin Kimani, shared the progress so far on the teachings done.</p><p>Here are those that have been done so far</p><p>In January handled – The New Creation and towards the end Purpose</p><p>In February handled= Prayer and towards the end The Word as the Foundation.</p><p>In March handled—The Holy Spirit</p><p>In April Handled—Grace versus the Law</p><p>It was therefore agreed to handle Faith series in May, Eternal Life Series in June, Believers Authority in July, and Prayer and Fasting in August.</p><p>The sessions in August were planned to have the teaching first and then pray towards the end to practice and actualize whatever has been learnt.</p><p>The discipleship guides were to be produced after the teaching has been done. They are to be added to the platform for easy access.</p><p><strong>MIN/8/4/25: FINANCE</strong></p><p>On finance, members agreed to register an M-Pesa till to facilitate collection of funds for the conference. James Kiarie was tasked with the responsibility to ensure the till was done and functional, i.e. integrated to the platform for accounting purposes.</p><p>The members agreed to continue contributing the KSH 2,000 at the end of every month to cater for upcoming needs especially on registration process.</p><p>The strategies to cater for the December conference were to be Fundraisers to be done after the sessions to promote the December event.</p><p>Budgeting of the Conference was tasked to the Conference committee.</p><p><strong>MIN/9/4/25: AUGUST PRAYERS</strong></p><p>Members agreed that the prayers should begin on 20th August, 2025 and end on Saturday, 23rd August 2025. Sunday service to be held at Gilgil Visions of Glory, The Grace Sanctuary Church after which members will have a common meal. The facilitation fee remains same at KSH 1,000 per individual which will cater for accommodation, and last meal.</p><p>Prayer Schedule for the same was to be planned and made ready prior to the conference by Paul Muteti. It was expected to be handed before or on 20th August 2025 before 2pm.</p><p>Traveling costs will be handled at an individual level.</p><p>The venue of the prayers remained to be Heavens Gate Prayer Mountain in Nakuru County.</p><p><strong>MIN/10/4/25: 2025 DECEMBER CONFERENCE.</strong></p><p>Members agreed that the conference in December to remain as previously planned with some few modifications and additional. The venue of the Conference changed from <i><strong>Agape Fellowship, Mitaboni</strong></i> as previously planned to <i><strong>Apostolic Faith Conference Centre, Kikopey Nakuru County.</strong></i> Members reached to this decision in order to stand independent of any church or denomination before the launch. Members paid a visit to the facility on Saturday, 21st April 2025 and were given a tour of the facility. The members were satisfied with the facilities in the place and decided to have it as the venue for the conference.&nbsp;</p><p>On charges of the Facility, Members agreed that Benjamin Kimani should meet with the relevant personnel and get a quote of their charges for proper planning. The conference facility offers everything including:</p><ol><li>The conference hall – with a capacity of 8000 seater.</li><li>The Accommodation Hostels – With the current capacity of 1800 beds.</li><li>Kitchen Facility – With all utensils, cooking materials etc.</li><li>Outdoor Activities</li><li>Outdoor Tents</li></ol><p>Members agreed to receive a quote first and then decide on the best approach to cater for the expenses.</p><p>The dates of the conference remained as planned running from <i><strong>1st December, 2025 to 6th December 2025.</strong></i> There was a slight change with the earlier on discussed schedule. The members agreed to finish up the program on<i><strong> 6th December climaxing with the Organization Launch.</strong></i> This was to allow the invited ministers to get time to travel back and minister the following Sunday in their churches. In addition, members agreed not to have a Worship Night on Friday Night to allow an early start of the launching celebration.</p><p>In the evening, members agreed to have <i><strong>round-tables</strong></i> to have a discussion on the Organization’s vision. These round tables will be focused on casting a vision of the Organization.&nbsp;</p><p>The minister during the conference were agreed to be as follows.&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Bishop Jim Maina – Who will minister the last two days, that is on Friday and the Launch service.</li><li>Apostle Nick Musembi – After confirming his available will be given a session as required. Paul Muteti was tasked with the responsibility to confirm his availabity.</li></ol><p>Members agreed to pray on the theme for the conference and to be discussed during the August Prayers.</p><p>Some of the objectives derived for the meeting were as follows:</p><ol><li>Vision Casting, mainly during the round tables.</li><li>Launching of the organization. To have an official launch of the organization.</li><li>Setting a foundation of the Christian faith.</li></ol><p>Members agreed to <i><strong>target 500 attendees</strong></i> to the conference of which <i><strong>150 of them to be High School Leavers</strong></i> and those in their final year.</p><p>Planning and Logistics were left to the committee.</p><p><strong>MIN/11/4/25: ORGANISATION REGISTRATION</strong>.</p><p>Members were earlier on requested to do research on the registration process and come with ideas in the next meeting. Members had succeeded to do a research and came to a consensus to register under <i><strong>Societies as a Welfare Society</strong></i>. This registration would call the organization to be registered as a Non-Profit Organization. The following were the reasons members settled for the Welfare Society.</p><ul><li>Based on the organization mission, it would be limiting to register the Organization under the Religious Organization. &nbsp;</li><li>A welfare society is a good one for development focused ministry, for instance under this the organization can stretch beyond the limits of religious organization to Education, Economic, Social, Youth empowerments, Games and Sports, Technology, Art and Entertainment etc.</li><li>Aligned with the legal structure of the country and fit for the mission of the organization</li></ul><p>The Kenyan Law provides two primary routes for non-profit organizations</p><ol><li>Register as an NGO under the NGO coordination act&nbsp;</li><li>Register as Non-profit company under the companies act.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;Registration process of the same was outlined to get the members to speed beginning with the requirements. (This is same for both of the above)</p><ul><li>Minimum of 3 Kenyan Trustees who must be Kenyan Citizens with clean legal records.</li><li>A constitution draft outlining, the name, mission, vision and objectives of the organization, Governance structure (the board), Dissolution clause.</li><li>Physical Address of the organization.</li></ul><p>For nonprofit companies there is an additional of the&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Memorandum &amp; articles of Association filed with the Kenya Companies Registry.</li><li>Company Limited by Guarantee. No shareholders; profits reinvested.</li></ul><p>The registration process was as follows.</p><ol><li>Name reservation<ol><li>Submit 3 proposed names to the NGO coordination board(Online)<ol><li>Members proposed the following names : <i><strong>Jesus Enthroned Network</strong></i></li><li><i><strong>Jesus Enthroned Network Global</strong></i></li><li><i><strong>Jesus Enthroned Global Network</strong></i></li></ol></li><li>Pay a name reservation fee of KSH 1,100</li><li>Wait 1-3 days for approval.</li></ol></li><li>Submission of Documents.<ol><li>Submit an Application Form for registry available online.</li><li>Submit Trustee details, Attaching copies of IDs, resumes, and KRA pins.</li><li>Submit a trustee declaration form available online.</li><li>Submit the constitution signed by all trustees</li><li>Pay a fee of KSH 22,600 for standard NGOs.</li></ol></li><li>Verification and Approval.<ol><li>Receive Certificate of Registration and an official NGO Number.</li></ol></li></ol><p>Members agreed to draft a constitution before beginning the process. James Kiarie was tasked with the responsibility of reserving the names for the organization.&nbsp;</p><p>Registration was set to be done as previously planned, June/July.</p><p><strong>MIN/12/4/25: REMAINING VISITS.</strong></p><p>As previously planned, members managed to pay a visit to Bishop Mungai, Pastor Cosmas Joseph and also Benjamin Parent. Though members said they would do a <i><strong>rein check on Benjamin’s Parents</strong></i> since the organization’s account were low and did not get the opportunity to purchase a token for them. Though the visits did not happen on the days planned due to some reasons.</p><p>On the remaining visits, that’s Visit to James’ Parents and pastor in Subukia, members <i><strong>postponed to September&nbsp;</strong></i>to give them time to cater for registration. In addition, James requested to postpone the visit to his parents till further notice due some family issues. The visit to the Pastor was set to be on September. Other visits to be discussed at a later meeting, i.e. visit to pastor Were.</p><p><strong>MIN/13/4/25: VISIT TO UGANDA (PHANEROO)</strong></p><p>Members agreed to pay a visit to <i><strong>Phaneroo Ministries International</strong></i> during their <i><strong>31st December 2025 Night of Prayer Vigil</strong></i>. The members agreed to leave on <i><strong>27th December 2025</strong></i> and be there for the week.&nbsp;</p><p>For Accommodation, Meals and Travelling costs, members agreed to contribute <i><strong>KSH 60,000 to a wallet</strong></i>. Fine-tuned details will be discussed at later dates on the visit but the contribution was to begin as early as the end of the meeting.</p><p><strong>MIN/14/4/25: ANY OTHER BUSINESS.</strong></p><p>With the meeting coming to an end, the floor was opened for any other business. Members were urged to invest both financially, coming from Benjamin Kimani, He urged members to have a culture of saving. Members were also encouraged to continually pray for the conference intentionally. In addition, members were reminded to mobilize for the conference.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>ADJOURNMENT.</strong></p><p>The meeting ended on 22nd April, 2025 with members departing to their respective homes and work places.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>CHAIRPERSON</td><td>SIGNATURE</td></tr><tr><td>BENJAMIN KIMANI</td><td>……………………………</td></tr><tr><td>SECRETARY</td><td>SIGNATURE</td></tr><tr><td>JAMES KIARIE(<i><strong>For the meeting)</strong></i></td><td>…………………………....</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>', '2025-04-27 14:26:16', 8, '2025-04-27 14:26:16'),
(2, 1010, '<p><strong>MINUTES FOR THE MEETING HELD ON 29-30TH DECEMBER 2024</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Members Present</strong></p><ol><li>Benjamin Kimani</li><li>Paul Muteti</li><li>James Kiarie</li></ol><p><strong>In Attendance</strong></p><ol><li>Timothy Mutisya</li></ol><h4>Meeting Agenda</h4><ol><li>Review of the HOFIRE 2024 Conference</li><li>Calendar of Events</li><li>JEN Meetings</li><li>Monthly meetings lineup</li><li>Tuesday Fellowships</li><li>Follow up and Discipleship</li><li>Finances</li><li>August Bootcamp</li><li>HOFIRE 2025 Conference</li><li>Devotionals</li><li>Doctrine Pamphlets</li><li>Roles and Duties</li><li>Registration</li><li>Any Other Business(A.O.B)</li></ol><h4>Opening.</h4><p>The meeting began on 29th December around 10pm with the three members present and continued up to 31st December. It was done in breaks to cater for activities that were to be done with the duration.</p><h4>MIN/1/12/24: REVIEW OF THE HOFIRE 2024 CONFERENCE.&nbsp;</h4><p>The members discussed the activities that took place during the Holy Ghost Fire and Revival (HOFIRE) Conference organized by Agape Fellowship Center youths at Mitaboni, Machakos County. The purpose of discussion was to point out the achievements and also mark the spots to be improved in the future if the organization was to plan for another conference as that. The achievements of the conference were as follows:</p><ol><li>The conference managed to get the youth leaders from within the area.</li><li>The conference raised a standard on the way of ministration among the youths.</li><li>The conference imparted lives of the youths to seek God in truth.</li><li>The conference managed to receive 18 new souls to Christ during Aps Nick Musembi’s ministration.</li></ol><p>The points of improvements noted down:</p><ol><li>Proper planning of a conference was need in the future to cater for<ol><li>Excellent and impactful music ministration.</li><li>Improvement of the coordination of activities not over burden other people while others are not rested.</li><li>Financial support to the conference.</li><li>Departmental organization such as the media, ushering etc.</li></ol></li><li>Mobilization of the local and exterior churches to attend the conferences.</li><li>Increase of laborers and ministers to the conferences.</li></ol><h4>MIN/2/12/24: CALENDAR OF EVENTS.</h4><p>Members agreed to have the following events in the year 2025.</p><ol><li>3 High School Missions mostly referred to as Weekend Challenges.</li><li>One conference for the youths.</li><li>One meeting with the laborers and ministers serving in the sub-committee planning for the conference.</li></ol><p>Below is the agreed plan for the events or the calendar of events.</p><ol><li>Weekend Challenge in March&nbsp;</li><li>Weekend Challenge in Term 2</li><li>Weekend Challenge in Term 2</li><li>Leadership Prayers/ Conference Prayers 5 days in August beginning 21&nbsp;</li><li>HOFIRE Conference 2025 in December</li></ol><p>Here is a visual representation of the calendar of events beginning from the most recent to the last.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>#</strong></td><td><strong>EVENT</strong></td><td><strong>DATES/MONTH</strong></td><td><strong>VENUE</strong></td><td><strong>DESCRIPTION</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>Weekend Challenge(High School)</td><td>1ST Week of March 2025</td><td><p>Katuanya High School</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td>To be confirmed by Paul Muteti</td></tr><tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>Weekend Challenge</td><td>Term 2 of Studies</td><td><p>Utumishi Schools&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td>To be Confirmed by Benjamin Kimani</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>Weekend Challenge</td><td>Term 2 of Studies</td><td><p>Makueni Boys High School</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td>To be confirmed by Paul Muteti</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>Bootcamp/Conference Prayers</td><td>21st – 24th August 2025</td><td><p>Heaven’s Gate Prayer Center.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></td><td><p>Members to have at least 1000 for accommodation purposes</p><p>The amount will cater for breaking fast on Sunday 24th also</p></td></tr><tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>HOFIRE 2025 CONFERENCE</td><td>1st – 7th&nbsp; December 2025</td><td>Agape Fellowship Center - Mitaboni</td><td>Registration amount of 1300 to cater for accommodation and meals.&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h4>&nbsp;</h4><h4>MIN/3/12/24: 2025 JEN ORGANISERS MEETINGS&nbsp;</h4><p>The members also agreed to plan several meetings within the year. The meetings include visiting the individual’s pastors and parents.&nbsp;</p><p>Below is the agreed times to visit the parents and the pastors.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>#</td><td>Meeting</td><td>Description</td><td>Period</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Visit Paul’s</td><td>Members paid a visit to pastor Daniel Kithusi pastor to Paul Muteti</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Visit to Benjamin’s(Gilgil)</td><td>Members agreed to pay a visit and seek blessing from Benjamin’s Parents, and Pastor(Pastor Cosmas Joseph)&nbsp;</td><td>Members to arrive on March 28 2025 and visit the pastor on 29/30th.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Visit to James’(Subukia)</td><td>Members agreed to pay a visit and seek blessing from James’ parents and pastor(Pastor Joseph Wachira)</td><td>Members arrive on 30th May 2025 and visit pastor on 31st/1st may 2025</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Visit to Paul’s</td><td>Members agreed to visit and receive blessing from Paul’s Parent in Mtito Andei</td><td>Members planned to visit on September 26-27th, 2025</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Visit Pastor Were</td><td>Members agreed to visit and receive a blessing from Pastor Were</td><td>Members chose dates between 28th -30th October 2025</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>MIN/4/12/24: MONTHLY MEETINGS LINE-UP</h4><p>Members agreed to have the following on- line meetings line up</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>#</td><td>MEETING</td><td>DESCRIPTION</td><td>TIME</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Every Tuesday</td><td>Online Fellowships open for all</td><td>8:00pm – 10:00pm</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Every Saturday</td><td>Meeting for members for prayers</td><td>9:00pm – 10:00pm</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Every 2nd Friday of the Month</td><td>Meeting for prayers for all – Coupled with a night vigil in a local church</td><td>9:00pm – 12:00 am</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Every 1st Saturday of the Month&nbsp;</td><td>Bible study for the members</td><td>9:00pm – 10:00pm</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Every 3rd Saturday of the month</td><td>Question and Answer Session – to be given in advance</td><td>8:30pm – 10:00pm</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Every last Tuesday&nbsp;</td><td>To have sessions to hold teachings outside doctrinal grounding to be done on two consecutive days</td><td>8:30pm – 10:00pm</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>MIN/5/12/24: TUESDAY FELLOWSHIPS</h4><p>Members agreed to have the following schedule for the Tuesday fellowships.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td>TIME</td><td>ACTIVITY</td></tr><tr><td>2000HRS – 2030HRS</td><td>Prayers for the members</td></tr><tr><td>2030HRS – 2110HRS</td><td>Prayers for all</td></tr><tr><td>2110HRS –&nbsp; 2200HRS</td><td>Word Session</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>MIN/6/12/24: FOLLOW UP AND DISCIPLESHIP</h4><p>Members agreed to have a site developed by February to handle follow up and discipleship of high school students. Members also agreed to do a follow up of those disciples in the WhatsApp group who have not been joining the meetings.</p><h4>MIN/7/12/24: FINANCES</h4><p>Members agreed to be depositing KSH 2,000 every month for the sake of creating a kitty fund. The fund will be used to cater for expenses used to purchase a token given to parents and pastors during visits. The kitty also will be a financial fund to support members and also events. The funds should be paid before or on the 10th Day of the month.</p><p>Members also agreed to individually build themselves financially through investments and other ways such as employment salaries.</p><h4>MIN/8/12/24: BOOTCAMP/CONFERENCE PRAYERS</h4><p>Members agreed to have prayers instead of a Bootcamp for youth leaders and C.U leaders. The prayers were meant to be dedicated for the conference to be held in December. Those who shall be ready to attend are estimated at 30 especially those who will be serving in the sub-committee preparing for the conference. The prayers shall be held at Heaven’s Gate Prayer Mountain which shall be a moment of fasting and later on break the fast at Gilgil. They are requested to carry with them KSH 1000 to cater for accommodation and breaking fast.</p><h4>MIN/9/12/24: DECEMBER CONFERENCE&nbsp;</h4><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Members agreed to have one conference to be held in December 2025, running from 1st to 7th. The members agreed to have a sub – committee to plan and ensure the success of the conference. As at the meeting the following were recommended to serve in the meeting.</p><ol><li>Paul Muteti – Sub Committee Chairperson</li><li>James Kiarie – Media Department</li><li>Dan Lochongo – Music Department</li></ol><p>The rest of the members of the committee were to be confirmed during the next meeting.</p><p>It was also agreed to cater for the meals and accommodation those attending should have a fee amount of KSH 1300. In order to support the conference the members agreed to have some merchandise and challenges, the merchandise was agreed to have some branded T-shirts for the conference.</p><p>&nbsp;The theme of the conference was set to be discussed during the next meeting and members encouraged to pray for the same.</p><p>The budgeted amount for the conference is running at KSH 500,000 having 100,000 set aside for ministers’ accommodation and appreciation.</p><p>The ministers who shall be present during the conference shall be&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Apostle Nick Musembi</li><li>The members individual pastors<ol><li>Pastor Daniel Kithusi</li><li>Pastor Cosmas Joseph</li><li>Pastor Joseph Wachira</li></ol></li></ol><h4>Launching</h4><p>Members chose to launch the organization during the conference immediately after worship experience. They agreed to have their individual pastors present to receive a commission and a blessing from them. The date for the launching shall be on 6th December 2025.</p><h4>Worship Experience</h4><p>The last day of the conference that is on 5th December, members agreed to have a worship experience in the night. The subcommittee was tasked with ensuring its success and also ensuring that everything was excellent.&nbsp;</p><h4>Mobilization</h4><p>Members agreed to do mobilization as from January 2025 and massive mobilizations in November.</p><h4>Prayers&nbsp;</h4><p>Members agreed to have a prayer retreat discussed above at heaven’s gate prayer mountain in August. In addition, the committee should include some prayers to be done virtually for the same through-out the year.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4>MIN/10/12/24: DEVOTIONALS</h4><p>Members agreed as part of discipleship to have quizzes for personal studies. The questions would demand the disciples to study the bible and later hand in notes of what they have studied.</p><h4>MIN/11/12/24: PUBLISHING DOCTRINE PAMPHLETS</h4><p>Members agreed to publish a document with the basic doctrines.&nbsp;</p><h4>MIN/12/12/24: ROLES AND DUTIES</h4><p>Members agreed to define roles and duties of the available people. The following was agreed while the empty or missing will be filled with time.</p><ol><li>Chairperson- Benjamin Kimani</li><li>Vice Chairperson – Paul Muteti</li><li>Secretary – Naomi</li><li>Vice Secretary – To be Filled</li><li>Treasurer – To be filled</li><li>Event Coordinator – Peter Thuita</li><li>Music Coordinator – Dan Lochongo</li><li>Media Coordinator – James Kiarie</li><li>Ushering Coordinator – To be filled</li></ol><p>Other roles to be assigned were as follows:</p><p>Teaching on Tuesdays – Benjamin Kimani and James Kiarie</p><p>Coordination of Prayers – Paul Muteti</p><h4>MIN/13/12/24: REGISTRATION</h4><p>Members agreed to continue with the research on registration and later on do registration on June.</p><p>The organogram will have been fully defined by then.</p><h4><strong>MIN/14/12/24: A.O.B</strong></h4><blockquote><p>Members agreed to have a logo design and defined their theme colors to be purple, gold and white. Also poster design for the conference.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote><h4>Close</h4><p>The meeting was adjourned on 31st December 1400hrs. The next meeting will be held during the First Weekend Challenge at Katuanya Girls High Schools.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '2025-04-27 17:53:55', 8, '2025-04-27 17:53:55'),
(4, 1028, '<h3>JESUS ENTHRONED NETWORK MINUTES FOR THE MEETING HELD ON SATURDAY, 19TH JULY 2025</h3><p>Members Present</p><ol><li>Benjamin Kimani</li><li>James Kiarie</li><li>Aron Ng’eno</li><li>Daniel Brian</li><li>Joshua Kiptoo</li><li>Gladwel Leparkeri</li><li>John Ngugi</li><li>Lewis Murimi</li><li>Amos Sila</li><li>Mark Kimani</li><li>Naomi Mwihaki</li></ol><p>Absent with Apologies</p><ol><li>Laban</li><li>Miriam Nkirote</li><li>Paul Muteti</li></ol><p>Agendas</p><ol><li>Preliminaries</li><li>Exhortation</li><li>Conference Budgeting</li><li>&nbsp;Launching</li><li>A.o.B</li><li>Adjournment</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>MIN/1/7/25: PRELIMINARIES AND MATTERS ARISING</h3><p>The meeting began with a session of prayer at 8:30pm. Benjamin Kimani began the meeting with the appreciation of every member that joined the session. The previous minutes were not read so the matters arising were not held.</p><h3>MIN/2/7/25: EXHORTATION</h3><p>Benjamin Kimani led through the prayer session, giving directions to the members to pray for the Jesus Enthroned Network and the Upcoming December Conference. He also shared an exhortation word&nbsp; of God.</p><h3>MIN/3/7/25: CONFERENCE BUDGETING</h3><ol><li><strong>Publicity and media budget estimation.</strong></li></ol><p>Amos Sila detailed costs for camera for both photography and videography, PC(Computer) Equipment, noting KSH 25,000 per day for a camcorder and photography camera, and KSH 3,500 per day per screen. Below is the summarized edition of the quote.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Equipment</strong></td><td><strong>Qty</strong></td><td><strong>Quote</strong></td><td><strong>Total</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Photography Camera</strong></td><td>1</td><td>2000</td><td>2000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Screens and Cables</strong></td><td>3</td><td>500</td><td>1500</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Full package (3 cameras, Pc and Wi-Fi)</strong></td><td>(Full Package)</td><td>25000</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; 2. &nbsp;Sound and Music Budget Estimation.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Mark Kimani provided a quote for sound equipment, ranging from KSH 5,000 to KSH 7,000 daily for premium sound quality. The equipment included in this quote were mixers, receivers and microphones. Benjamin Kimani also mentioned consulting with their pastor, who introduced him to person who quoted KSH 10,000 a day for drums and piano. He was requested by the members to enquire on the package of the instrument provided and whether the mixer offered digital or analog signals.</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;3. &nbsp; Meals, Accommodation and Facilities Budget Estimation</strong></p><p>Benjamin Kimani shared the initial quotation for five days, covering food, accommodation, and facilities for 500 people in 5days. The contribution per person based on this quote was to be KSH 2,100. ­ As earlier agreed members decided to work with a three-day budget, giving the contribution amount to 1260. The members agreed instead of asking attendees to contribute the KSH 1260, to ask KSH 1500 to cater for extra budgets, the media and the music budgets etc.</p><p>The discussion on shortening the days to three made the shift for the conference start dates, which were said to be from 3rd December, 2025 to 6th December, 2025. Attendees would arrive from Wednesday Evening, to Saturday.</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; 4. &nbsp; Event Budget and the Duration Adjustment</strong>.</p><p>The total amount contributed by members would be KSH 750,000. Below was the budgeting for the event.</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Budget Description</strong></td><td><strong>Amount</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Media Budget Estimate</strong></td><td>50,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Honorariums and Minister’s Appreciation</strong></td><td>50,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sound/Music Budget Estimate</strong></td><td>50,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Accommodation/Meals/Facility</strong></td><td>630,000</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Launching Budget Estimate</strong></td><td>30,000</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>As per the budget above, there was a deficit of KSH 60,000.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;5. &nbsp;Members Participation on ways of getting the budgets.</strong></p><p>James Kiarie suggested in order to cater for the extra budget, to have attendees contribute 1600 which would cut the cost in a KSH 10,000 deficit, while Aron Ngeno proposed to maintain the contribution at 1500 per attendee, emphasizing the need to consider that they would be taking care of their travel costs. Daniel Brian also seconded Aron, while giving the members an opportunity to find ways to ver the deficit for their side. Lewis Murimi and Benjamin Kimani discussed the idea of selling merchandise like t-shirts or caps for branding and marketing, with attendees purchasing them voluntarily.</p><h3>MIN/4/7/25: LAUNCH EVENT TIMING AND LOGISTICS</h3><p>There was a discussion on the timing of the launch event on 6th December, 2025. Benjamin Kimani suggested starting the launch early, around 9:00AM, and finishing by 1:00PM or 2:00PM. For those who would be traveling to far destinations after the launch they could spend the night in the facility and then later on depart on Sunday 7th December morning. Still also on the launching event budget, Naomi Mwihaki was tasked with confirming a quote on decoration for the event, while Lewis Murimi and Joshua Kiptoo were tasked with getting a quote on cakes and the snacks for the event.&nbsp;</p><p>The committee was to get a good estimate of the budge required in the next meeting. James Kiarie pledged to cater for the branding of pens to be distributed during the conference. The number of pens agreed on were 600.</p><h3>MIN/5/7/25: ANY OTHER BUSINESS</h3><ol><li><strong>Roles and Responsibilities for the conference.</strong></li></ol><p>John Ngugi suggested to delegate people that would server during the conference, emphasizing the need of the collaboration between the hosts and the conference organizer. For instance, in welfare ensuring that there is good communication between the chefs and us the conference organizers for proper meal times etc, also in other departments such as media, ushering, and moderation. Benjamin Kimani emphasized on this and confirmed that it would be done during the August Prayers happening at the Heavens Gate Prayer Mountain.</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; 2. &nbsp;Conference Mobilization and Financial Support.</strong></p><p>Benjamin Kimani emphasized on importance of mobilization and note that there isn’t a significant burden on their side to raise the finances. They suggested supporting the individuals who might struggle to afford the full amount required for the conference, mentioning personal plans to top up contributions for such attendees.</p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;3. &nbsp;Miscellaneous</strong></p><p><i><strong>Registration and Legal documents.</strong></i></p><p>Benjamin Kimani update members on the organization’s registration, confirming that all documents are ready and urged members who committed to contributing financially to do so by 1st August 2025.&nbsp;</p><p><i><strong>Logo Design and Feedback</strong></i></p><p>Lewis Murimi confirmed that a concept had been made and sent to James Kiarie, who acknowledged receiving the design. James Kiarie explained that the sketch was just a concept representing their mission and vision of a Kingdom united in purpose, also incorporating unity and teamwork, and state that the final logo will include designed color. Aron Ng’eno suggested having different design options.</p><p><i><strong>August Prayers and Conference Preparations</strong></i></p><p>Benjamin noted that many had registered for the August prayer but encouraged others to reached out if they hadn’t. They planned for the attendees to visit the conference venue on a Saturday after the August Prayers to familiarize themselves with the location and aid the media efforts.&nbsp;</p><p>Benjamin also noted that Bishop Jim Maina will be the guest minister for the conference and he would be visiting him in August to confirm attendance and get the solid dates that he will be available.</p><h3>MIN/6/7/2025: Adjournment</h3><p>Being no other business, the meeting was adjourned at 10:15pm. The next meeting will be held during the August Prayers at Heavens Gate during the prayers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Chairperson</strong></td><td><strong>Name</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>………………………………………………………………………….</strong></td><td>Benjamin Kimani</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Secretary</strong></td><td>Name</td></tr><tr><td><strong>…………………………………………………………………………</strong></td><td>Naomi Mwihaki</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '2025-09-02 19:23:18', 8, '2025-09-02 19:23:18'),
(5, 1036, '<p>JESUS ENTHRONED NETWORK MINUTES FOR THE MEETING HELD ON 2ND SEPTEMBER 2025 1800HRS</p><p><strong>Members Present</strong></p><ol><li>Benjamin Kimani</li><li>Paul Muteti</li><li>James Kiarie</li></ol><p><strong>Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>Opening</li><li>Previous minutes</li><li>Matters Arising</li><li>Conference Sporsorship</li><li>Organization Registration</li><li>Conference Marketing Tools</li><li>Launching</li><li>Any Other Business</li><li>Decisions Made</li><li>Adjournment</li></ol><p>MIN/1/BD/9/2025: Opening</p><p>The meeting began at around 6.00pm with a 5 minutes session of prayer.</p><p>MIN/2/BD/9/2025: READING OF THE PREVIOUS MINUTES</p><p>The previous minutes of the conference committee meeting were read and confirmed.</p><p>MIN/3/DB/9/2025: MATTERS ARISING</p><ol><li><strong>Accommodation on the Last</strong></li></ol><p>A concern was raised on the previous agreement to allow those travelling far distances after the launching event in December to spend the night the Conference facility. The concern was on whether there was a rise on the conference expenditure. It was confirmed that what would rise is the cost on meals for those spending the night, only to cater for their supper and or(breakfast Sunday morning)</p><ol><li><strong>Roles and Duties for the conference</strong></li></ol><p>The members the need to have people serve in various departments during the conference. The following were the departments that were found crucial for the conference.</p><ol><li>Ushering</li><li>Logistics</li><li>Media</li><li>Welfare</li><li>Moderation</li></ol><p>Members agreed for the department heads, to utilize those serving in the committee. For the other attendees who want to serve, get a list of them who want to serve through a form.</p><ol><li><strong>Conference Support and Sponsorship</strong></li></ol><p>Members discussed on the sponsorship for the conference. Members agreed to have an attendee-based sponsorship that would seem convenient and favorable to market to external partners. (Those not associated directly with the activities of the conference).</p><ol><li><strong>Organization Registration</strong></li></ol><p>Members confirmed the amount available for the registration and also confirmed that they would personally start getting the documents necessary for the registration process.</p><ol><li><strong>Report on the August Prayer</strong></li></ol><p>Benjamin Confirmed that there a fairly good attendance to the August Prayers held at Heavens Gate Conference. Overall today number who attended was 17, 7 of them arriving on the first day, 8 of them joining on the second day (Thursday), and 2 Join on the last day(Friday).</p><p>MIN/4/BD/2025: ORGANISATION NAME.</p><p>Members agreed to settle with the name ‘Jesus Enthroned Network’ and also in the future consider a change if need arises.</p><p>MIN/5/BD/2025: CURRICULUM FOR THE NEXT YEARS MENTORSHIP</p><p>Members proposed to have a mentorship program next year to empower and build the form 4 leaver, those who complete their secondary education. This mentorship would be centered on the purpose identification and empowerment. Members agreed to do research and have a discussion on it during their next meeting. There was also raised the devotionals during the discussion of this agenda. Members so it fit to include the discussion in their next meeting and also research on a strategy to ensure success and consistency.</p><p>MIN/6/BD/CONFERENCE UPDATES</p><p>Members confirmed that the conference dates will be from 3rd to 6th of December with the last day scheduling for the Organization launch. The venue remained as discussed at , Gilgil Apostolic Faith Church Conference Facility in Kekopey, Gilgil Nakuru County.</p><p>On mobilization members agreed to have and begin mobilization immediately. &nbsp;On accounting members agreed to allow Paul to check out on the paybill/till number registration as he had suggested.&nbsp;</p><p>On the activities to be scheduled for the conference include.</p><ol><li>Teachings.</li><li>Q&amp;A or Panel discussions</li><li>Workshops</li><li>Peer to Peer talks/Bible study.</li><li>Games and sports.</li></ol><p>On scheduling members agreed to check on the hours they shall have during the conferene ie the time available.&nbsp;</p><p>MIN/7/BD/2025: AOB</p><ol><li><strong>Agenda for the conference Committee next meeting</strong><ol><li>Partnerships and Sponsorship</li><li>Mobilization</li><li>Duties and Responsibilities</li><li>Feedback from previous meeting</li><li>Conferece Extra cost acquisition</li><li>Deadlines</li><li>A.OB</li></ol></li><li><strong>Payers</strong><ol><li>Paul mentioned of a planned joint prayer for 3 hours coming up.</li><li>Paul also exhorted the members urging them to continually pray for the conference.</li></ol></li></ol><p>MIN/8/BD/2025: DECISIONS</p><p>The next meeting was decided to be on 8th of September 2025, at 6pm, while the meeting for conference committee was re-confirmed to be on 4th of September 2025.</p><p>MIN/9/BD/2025: ADJOURNMENT</p><p>The meeting was ended with a prayer made by Paul. The next meeting will be on 8th September 2025 at 6pm.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Benjamin Kimani&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;…………………………………………</p><p>Paul Muteti&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ………………………………………..</p><p>James Kiarie&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;……………………………………………</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '2025-09-09 20:02:32', 8, '2025-09-09 20:02:32');
INSERT INTO `meeting_minutes` (`id`, `meeting_id`, `minutes`, `created_at`, `personnel`, `update_at`) VALUES
(6, 1037, '<p>JESUS ENTHRONED NETWORK MINUTES FOR THE COMMITTEE MEETING HELD ON WEDNESDAY, 3RD SEPTEMBER 2025, VIA GOOGLE MEET FROM 8:30 P.M. – 10:38 P.M.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MEMBERS PRESENT</p><p>1.Benjamin Kimani</p><p>2.James Kiarie</p><p>3.Paul Muteti</p><p>4.Brian Kiprotich</p><p>5.Daniel Brian</p><p>6.Gladwel Leparkeri</p><p>7.Amos Sila</p><p>8.John Ngugi</p><p>9.Joshua Kiptoo</p><p>10Joy Wanjiku</p><p>11.Lewis Murimi</p><p>12.Laban</p><p>13.Mark Kimani</p><p>14.Miriam Nkirote</p><p>15.Tabitha Muthoni</p><p>16.Teresiah</p><p>17.Victor Mutinda</p><p>18.Aaron Ng’eno</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>AGENDAS&nbsp;</p><p>1.Opening and Welcoming Remarks</p><p>2.The Word</p><p>3.Review of the Previous Minutes</p><p>4.Preliminaries and Feedback on the Previous Meeting</p><p>5.Partnerships and Sponsorship for the Conference</p><p>6.Conference Mobilization</p><p>7.Conference Duties and Mobilization</p><p>8.Conference Extra Budget Acquisition</p><p>9.Deadlines</p><p>10.Any Other Business</p><p>11.Closing Remarks</p><p>12.Adjournment</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>MIN 1/8/2025: OPENING AND WELCOMING REMARKS</h3><p>The meeting began at 8.30pm with Paul Muteti welcoming everyone to the meeting while thanking and appreciating the members for their punctuality. He also led through a prayer session while giving the prayer directors.&nbsp;</p><h3>MIN 2/8/2025: EXHORTATION</h3><p>Benjamin Kimani shared briefly on the vision of the Organization emphasizing the future which depends on the fulfilment of purpose to every individual associated with Jesus Enthroned Network. He also pointed out the importance of getting to understand of their identity in God, their purpose and how to fulfil it. Benjamin emphasized the need for patience, diligence for the fulfilment of the vision. The growth of the network meant that everyone in it grows in their personal lives. He ended by affirming that we should not loose sight of where we are headed to, since we are not where we started.</p><h3>MIN 3/8/2025: REVIEW OF THE PREVIOUS MINUTES</h3><p>The minutes for the previous meeting were read through by Naomi Mwihaki and confirmed by Lewis Murimi and Joshua Kiptoo.</p><h3>MIN 4/8/2025: PRELIMINARIES AND FEEDBACK ON THE PREVIOUS MEETING</h3><ol><li><strong>Benjamin Kimani Report and Feedback</strong></li></ol><p>Benjamin Kimani reported that he had met Bishop Jim Maina in Kagio, who is the guest minister for the conference. Bishop Jim confirmed that he would be available on Thursday, 4th December 2025 and leave on Friday, which meant he would not be available during the launching. The reason is because in his local church, he will be having a Conference during the same week.</p><ol><li><strong>Media Report by Sila Mulwa</strong></li></ol><p>Sila Mulwa was to give a report on the quote for conference budget for the media and publicity. Sila reported engaging with Brian Koton, Emidge Creatives director who quoted for the necessary equipment needed for the conference in the media department. The quotation totaled to Ksh 33,500 for 4 days. The cost was exclusive of the transport, tripod stand and 2 Computers (PCs). Sila promised to provide 1 computer, while Mark and Steve will provide the other one. This would eliminate the cost of hiring computers. For a timer, members agreed to settle with a monitor which would be provided by Benjamin. A concern was raised whether the labor costs were on the provider or the Organization. It was confirmed that all the equipment would be handled by JEN.&nbsp;</p><p>The quotation has been attached at the end of the minutes.</p><ol><li><strong>Launching Decoration Report by Naomi Mwihaki.</strong></li></ol><p>Naomi Mwihaki reported on decoration for the conference consulting with Rael Nzeli (Captain) a decoration manager. Rael confirmed the cost to range between Ksh. 10,000 – 30,000 depending with the design of the decoration. Naomi was tasked to liaise with Rael and get quotations for different options or prices within 15,000 – 20,000 and confirm if transport and labor are included in the quote.</p><ol><li><strong>Report on Cakes for the Launching by Joshua Kiptoo and Lewis Murimi</strong>&nbsp;</li></ol><p>Joshua Kiptoo and Lewis Murimi reported that precuts cost were in about Ksh. 140 quoting a cost of Ksh 7,000 for the total budget. Benjamin Kimani suggested allocating Ksh 10,000 to include the miscalleneous costs. James Kiarie suggested that the members should check out for quotations from different bakers instead of working with rough figures. Sila also recommended using Bakers within Nakuru in order to get freshly baked cakes and reduce on transport costs. Mark Kimani was tasked alongside Joshua and Lewis to get quotations to be shared during the next meeting.</p><h3>MIN 5/8/2025: PARTNERSHIPS AND SPONSORSHIP FOR THE CONFERENCE</h3><p>Benjamin Kimani re-affirmed that the target for the conference is 500 young people, this number includes at least 200 young people who will have completed their secondary education (High School Graduands). He suggested that committee members to begin personal pledges, i.e. commitments towards sponsoring those who will not be able to raise the amount for the registration. Afterwards, partners and friends will be invited to support.</p><p>For accountability, sponsorship will be both on cash basis and attendees basis. Partners will sponsor either through cash commitment or attendee commitment. For partners outside the committee their commitment will be allocated to specific people and will be available upon request by the specific partner.</p><p>On how to collect and document the collections, there were several suggestions, James Kiarie suggested having an online form where partners can fill their commitments and can be retrieved for documenting. Naomi Mwihaki suggested that the committee members to commit their sponsorship during the meeting, Tabitha Kimani suggested that the partners to commit in cash basis and then later on calculate the number of people sponsored. It was agreed that a form should be made for the members to commit their contributions, the form should have both cash and attendee sponsorship, and was to be ready by 5th September 2025.</p><h3>MIN 6/8/2025: CONFERENCE MOBILIZATION</h3><p><strong>Ways to mobilize</strong></p><ol><li>High School Reach-out.</li></ol><p>Benjamin Kimani stated that he would be reaching out to his former high school and other high schools targeting CU officials, and or the form fours. Mark Kimani suggested using legal documents to invite and gain trust from the school heads, this was linked to the registration of the organization. James Kiarie suggested that instead of the legal document we should have fliers which are favorable for marketing purposes than the legal documents. It was then agreed to have fliers for the conference which would be used to market.</p><ol><li>Youth Fellowships reach-out</li></ol><p>James Kiarie suggested mobilizing through various church youth groups and fellowships, especially those that members fellowship in. Lewis confirmed that he would reach out to his home church</p><ol><li>Members within Jesus Enthroned</li></ol><p>Benjamin Kimani stated that all members within JEN, those who have ever joined in our session, to be called to confirm their availability for the conference. Naomi also suggested using the High School students within to mobilize in their schools. Members emphasized that the fliers should be ready soon to facilitate smooth mobilization.</p><p>Aaron suggested the meeting links to include collecting data to capture those currently in their High School level of student. James Kiarie stated that he would look into it and give feedback.</p><h3>MIN 7/8/2025: CONFERENCE DUTIES AND MOBILIZATION</h3><p>As it was earlier found, there was need to have people serve in various departments. The department heads that were to server in various departs were decided to be:</p><ol><li><strong>Music – Miriam Nkirote</strong></li><li><strong>Ushering – Brian Kiprotich</strong></li></ol><p>These will form the structures necessary in their departments. A call to serve form will be shared to the group after mobilization, after which the information collected will be shared to the department leaders. The leaders will have the opportunity to contact them and then set the necessary structures in preparation of the conference.</p><h3>MIN 8/8/2025: CONFERENCE EXTRA BUDGET ACQUISITION</h3><p>Benjamin Kimani noted that there was a deficit of Ksh. 60,000 in the conference budget. Members had earlier agreed to used merchandise to contribute towards the deficit. Merchandise was to be voluntary but the committee members were encouraged to at least purchase on of the merchandise.&nbsp;</p><p>Another means to fetch the deficit would be through weekly contributions towards the conference at the end of the Tuesday fellowships.&nbsp;</p><h3>MIN 9/8/2025: DEADLINES</h3><p>The members agreed to set deadlines for the following</p><figure class=\"table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Activity/Requirement</strong></td><td><strong>Deadline</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Fliers</td><td>12th September</td></tr><tr><td>Posters</td><td>5th September</td></tr><tr><td>Feedback and Reports on conference budgeting quotatios</td><td>10th September</td></tr><tr><td>Partnership Form</td><td>5th September</td></tr><tr><td>Service Form</td><td>12th September</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>MIN 10/8/2025: ANY OTHER BUSINESS</h3><p><strong>Logo</strong></p><p>James Kiarie reported that the media team were in the last phase of coming up with a logo. He shared the concepts that were available at the time.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Registration</strong></p><p>Benjamin Kimani stated that these will be included in fliers and posters.</p><p><strong>Conference name and Theme</strong></p><p>Miriam Nkirote enquired about JEN registration. Pastor Benjamin said only charges remain pending.</p><p><strong>Pledge Follow-Up</strong></p><p>Miriam Nkirote suggested reminders for pledges. Benjamin Kimani responded that a finance team will be formed to handle follow-ups.</p><h3>MIN 11/8/2025: CLOSING REMARKS</h3><p>Benjamin Kimani thanked members for attending. He invited brief greetings from Laban, Joy, Daniel Brian, and Brian Kiprotich.</p><h3>MIN 12/8/2025: ADJOURNMENT</h3><p>There being no other business, members shared the Grace. The meeting was adjourned at 10:38 p.m.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Next Meeting: Wednesday, 10th September 2025, at 8:30 p.m.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Chairperson:</p><p>&nbsp;<i><strong>Benjamin Kimani</strong></i></p><p>Signature:&nbsp;</p><p>……………………………………………</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Secretary:&nbsp;</p><p><i><strong>Naomi Mwihaki</strong></i></p><p>Signature:&nbsp;</p><p>…………………………………………….</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '2025-09-10 09:59:19', 8, '2025-09-10 09:59:19');
